NOTES:\P\pxi-3,l3,t2.14103;1.^IALL PIPE SIZES ARE ASME OD BASED\P2.^IVESSEL DESIGNED AS PER ASME SEC VIII DIV.01 STANDARD  \P3.^IALL CLEAN UTILITY AND PROCESS PIPES & FITTINGS ARE BS4825 STANDARD \P4.^IFOR BLACK UTILITY, PIPES & FITTINGS WILL BE AS PER B
  3
S4825 STANDARD \P5.^IALL EQUIPMENT ARE DESIGNED FOR NON-FLAMEPROOF AREA \P6.^IALL TEMPERATURE SENSORS WILL BE FOR THE RANGE OF 0 TO 150 °C. SIMPLEX SENSORS ARE CONSIDERED FOR ALL TEMPERATURE SENSORS.  \P7.^IVENT FILTER INTEGRITY TO BE CHECKED BEFORE STE
  3
RILIZATION AND AFTER BATCH IS OVER (EMPTY VESSEL). IN BOTH CASES DIFFUSED AIR & FLUID SHALL BE TAKEN IN VESSEL \P8.^IPLC SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH 20% SPARE I/O FOR BOTH ANALOGUE AND DIGITAL SIGNAL. PANEL IS PROVIDED WITH 20% FREE SPACE  \P9.^ISTIRRER RPM
  3
 WILL BE BASED ON FEEDBACK RECEIVED FROM VFD & WITH RPM SENSOR & TRANSMITTER CONSIDERED{\fTrebuchet MS|b0|i0|c0|p34; } \P10.^I CUSTOMER TO USE INSTALLATION  TOOL & TIGHTENING TOOL FOR MALE BEARING AND MIXING HEAD OF MAGNETIC MIXER, INCASE ON ANY MAINT
  3
ENANCE. ALL TOOLS ARE IN CLIENT'S SCOPE \P11.^I TRANSFER IN LINE FOR MANUFACTURING VESSEL, CIP & SIP SHALL BE DONE ALONG WITH THE VESSEL USING SPOOL PIECE, CONSIDERING NON STERILE ADDITION \P12.^I CONDUCTIVITY SENSOR PROVIDED AT DRAIN HEADER IN RESPECT
  3
IVE ROOMS FOR MANUFACTURING & FILTRATION VESSEL \P13.^I TRANSFER LINE FROM MANUFACTURING VESSEL TO HOLDING VESSEL SHALL BE SUBJECTED TO CIP IN ONCE THROUGH MODE. CLEANING VALIDATION IS TIMER BASED    \P14.^I ALL AIR FILTERS AND ALL LIQUID FILTERS CARTR
  3
IDGES ARE IN CLIENT'S SCOPE \P15.^I SLOPE FOR PIPING WILL BE CONSIDERED AS PER ASME BPE STANDARDS \P16.^I ALL COMPONENTS MARKED IN GREY ARE IN CLIENT'S SCOPE \P17.^I PRESSURE HOLD TEST OF TRANSFER LINE WILL BE DONE ALONG WITH VESSEL.\P18.^I ALL VESSELS A
  3
RE SUBJECTED TO ESIP BY PASSING PURE STEAM INTO THE VESSEL. \P19.^I SS 304 RACK TO BE PROVIDED FOR HOLDING SENSORS WHEN NOT IN USED\P20.^ICIP SHALL BE DONE BY WFI ONLY FOR ALL VESSELS AND TRANSFER LINES. AS PER DISCUSSION WITH CLIENT ONE OF THE PRODUCT
  1
 REQUIRED ACID & ALKALI DOSING FOR CIP THATS WHY DOSING BOTTLES \P\pi0;KEPT ON CIP SKID
